{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26277 - PROTEIN:5832",
  "verbalization": "Stecholide I appears to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a protein that is targeted by multiple compounds, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate. These compounds are all targets of HuT78, suggesting a potential mechanism where Stecholide I indirectly influences HuT78 through the activation or inhibition of this sialyltransferase. The evidence indicates that Stecholide I may act as a modulator of the sialyltransferase pathway, which is involved in the synthesis of sialic acid, a critical component in cell surface glycoconjugates. The presence of multiple targets in the sialyltransferase pathway, coupled with the shared target HuT78, supports the hypothesis that Stecholide I interacts with this pathway to influence HuT78's function. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Stecholide I to exert its effects through a complex, multi-target mechanism that involves the sialyltransferase enzyme.",
